  "id": "temporal-precedence",
  "term": "temporal precedence",
  "definition": "Temporal precedence means that one factor or process happens earlier in time than another, so its timing can be examined as potentially coming before later outcomes. In mental health research, longitudinal studies are used to clarify whether a variable precedes later symptoms or related experiences.",
